WEBVTT

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:05.480
I wonder what it will be?

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.440
This week, it's this!

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:09.390
What is this?

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:11.490
It says Earthbound Immortal.  
Does that mean it's a god?

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:13.090
Can it be defeated?

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:14.990
It's going to appear in this episode!

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:26.160
Crow!

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:28.680
Crow!

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:34.450
Where's Yusei?

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.560
Yusei!

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:47.880
Why is Yusei participating in a Riding Duel?

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.630
Who's the opponent?

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:50.830
It's Kiryu.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.110
Kiryu?

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:55.750
You mean Kyosuke Kiryu?

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:57.010
Why him?

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:59.550
Crow, what's going on?

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:02.270
I don't know either.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:06.930
However, I know for sure that the 
flaming race course isn't Solid Vision.

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:13.520
And this is a real duel where 
Yusei is risking his life.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.370
What's wrong?  Your D-Wheel is in pain!

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:26.600
Keep it together until this duel is over!

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:46.670
Looking over a vast distance

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:51.770
I realized my field of vision was narrow

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:56.680
Even if it’s easier to throw myself away

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:01.450
I want to survive to the best of my abilities

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:06.810
No matter how bad today is

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:11.800
There’s still the faintest light

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:17.200
All I have to do tomorrow

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:21.270
Is light it myself

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:26.270
I test myself so I won’t stop or vanish

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:31.240
Even if I get countless scars

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:37.540
I ride wishing for the 
arrival of a true tomorrow

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:41.520
Today will never exist again

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:47.430
So I won’t stop or vanish

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:17.240
Tremble with Fear!  Earthbound 
Immortal Ccapac Apu

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:19.360
Yusei!

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:22.630
What's wrong?

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:26.400
During this End Phase, 
Power Baton's effect ends.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:31.500
Therefore, Hundred-Eyes Dragon's attack 
points decrease from 5300 to 3000!

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:37.690
Kiryu's handless combo is scary 
because when he has zero cards

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:41.690
in his hand, he can use the effects 
of monsters in his graveyard.

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:44.560
However, Yusei should be 
good enough to beat this.

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:47.670
My turn!

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:54.160
When he has zero cards in his hand, his 
handless combo allows him to activate monster effects.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.620
But there's something I can do!

00:03:56.950 --> 00:04:00.260
When monsters are only on 
the opponent's side of the

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:04.260
field, I can Special Summon 
this card as a Level 4 monster!

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:06.490
Come, Level Warrior!

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:15.260
Then I Normal Summon Hyper Synchron!

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:25.020
Hyper Synchron tunes Level Warrior!

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:34.030
The wishes come together to form a new 
shining star!  Become the path that lights the way!

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:35.470
Synchro Summon!

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:38.180
Soar, Stardust Dragon!

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:43.170
That dragon is proof that you're a Signer!

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:45.400
Come and get me, Yusei!

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:48.090
Next is Hyper Synchron's monster effect!

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:50.600
When Hyper Synchron was used to summon a

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:53.600
Synchro Monster, that monster 
gains 800 attack points!

00:04:55.030 --> 00:05:00.720
All right!  Stardust Dragon's attack points are 
greater than Hundred-Eyes Dragon's attack points!

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:02.100
Nicely done, Yusei!

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:05.290
But what will he do about the handless combo?

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:10.740
Battle!  Stardust Dragon, roar!

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.440
Shooting Sonic!

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:19.060
Hundred-Eyes Dragon gains the monster effect 
of Infernity Guardian that's in my graveyard!

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:24.380
Due to this, it won't be destroyed in battle!

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:27.360
However, you'll still take battle damage!

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:34.600
That's a nice amount of damage, Yusei!

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:38.150
Let's keep having fun and 
shave away our lives!

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:45.780
Since Stardust Dragon dealt battle damage, 
the Continuous Trap Shard of Hope activates.

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:48.350
I draw one card from my deck.

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:53.130
If that card is a trap card, I can 
activate it by destroying Shard of Hope.

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:57.210
I'm betting everything on this draw!

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:03.480
I did it!

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:07.180
My combo becomes a path that lights the way!

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:12.870
I destroy Shard of Hope 
to activate this card.

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:16.010
I activate the trap card Miracle Locus!

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:21.440
You get to draw one card, 
and my Stardust Dragon gains

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:25.440
1000 attack points and can attack 
for a second time this turn!

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:27.910
Now draw, Kiryu!

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:30.330
How dare you!

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:39.960
Nicely done!  He can only activate his 
handless combo when he has zero cards in his hand!

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:42.590
I see!  That's why he 
forced him to draw a card!

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:44.950
Go!  The second battle!

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:47.270
Roar!  Shooting Sonic!

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:56.280
All right!

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:58.730
He destroyed Hundred-Eyes Dragon!

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:02.190
Now his handless combo is completely broken!

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:10.710
When Hundred-Eyes Dragon is destroyed, I 
select one card in my deck and add it to my hand.

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:17.160
This is the final blow!  I activate my trap!

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:19.520
Synchro Destructor!

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:22.500
When my Synchro Monster destroys 
your monster in battle,

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.800
you take damage equal to half 
that monster's attack points.

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:30.620
Furthermore, if the destroyed monster was a 
Synchro Monster, you take that damage again!

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:35.830
All right!  Half of Hundred-Eyes 
Dragon's attack points are 1500!

00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:38.820
Taking that twice would 
be 3000 points of damage!

00:07:39.130 --> 00:07:40.550
Yusei wins!

00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:43.730
Yusei planned his combo excellently.

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:46.420
You're incredible, Yusei!

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:52.690
How dare you, Yusei!

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:54.340
Just kidding.

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:57.490
I activate my trap Damage Translation!

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:01.110
This halves the damage I 
take from card effects!

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:16.210
That was good damage, Yusei!

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:19.560
He survived!

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:22.260
But Kiryu has no more 
monsters left on his field.

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:26.570
Yusei has Stardust Dragon that's 
been powered up by Hyper Synchron.

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:30.810
Even if Kiryu Special Summons 
a monster, Yusei has

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:35.410
Scrap-Iron Scarecrow set on his 
field, so he can negate his attack.

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:39.290
At first glance, it looks like Yusei 
is guaranteed to win.  However…

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:45.310
There must be something special about the 
card that Kiryu just added to his hand.

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:49.580
On the next turn, my Speed Counter will be 8.

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:56.020
If I activate the Speed Spell Final Attack, 
Stardust Dragon's attack points will be doubled.

00:08:57.320 --> 00:08:58.170
I end my tu-

00:08:57.920 --> 00:08:59.790
During the End Phase!

00:09:00.070 --> 00:09:03.970
Damage Translation's other effect activates.

00:09:03.970 --> 00:09:07.500
During the End Phase, I can 
Special Summon the same number of

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:10.980
Ghost Tokens as the number of times 
I took damage from card effects.

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:12.630
What are you planning to do?

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:18.530
What's so funny?

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:20.920
I can't stop laughing!

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:25.350
Thanks to you destroying 
Hundred-Eyes Dragon, I was

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:29.770
able to add the strongest 
Dark Signer card to my hand.

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:30.970
What?

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:33.410
It's showtime!

00:09:36.020 --> 00:09:36.980
What?

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:42.610
Who are they?

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:44.060
They're people!

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:46.480
There are people in the geoglyph flames!

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:48.780
Who are they?

00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:55.240
They're the people who 
vanished from Satellite.

00:09:56.830 --> 00:10:01.300
You were the ones who made the 
Satellite citizens vanish?

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:04.490
It's my turn.

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:08.000
But due to Power Baton's 
effect, I can't draw.

00:10:10.390 --> 00:10:13.050
Kiryu!  What did you do to them?

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:19.030
They're going to be sacrificed to this card.

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:21.450
Sacrificed?

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:26.180
With their sacrifices, this 
card gains the power of a god!

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:29.190
I release the two Tokens.

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:45.290
What?

00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:49.790
What's happening?

00:10:50.050 --> 00:10:52.680
I sacrifice their souls.

00:10:52.950 --> 00:10:57.920
Descend, Earthbound Immortal Ccapac Apu!

00:11:26.130 --> 00:11:27.200
Impossible!

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:32.850
No way…

00:11:42.100 --> 00:11:44.760
That monster is humongous!

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:51.090
Yusei, taste the curse of the dead!

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:53.450
My Earthbound Immortal Ccapac Apu!

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:57.470
Swing the steel hammer of justice 
on our enemy, the Signers!

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:04.430
Stardust!

00:12:08.550 --> 00:12:11.030
What?  Scrap-Iron Scarecrow!

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:18.500
You fool!  Do you really think such cheap 
tricks will work against an Earthbound Immortal?

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:24.720
Damn!  I can't even defend 
with a monster or a trap!

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:28.700
Yusei!

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:29.960
Yusei!

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:47.310
Yusei!

00:12:47.310 --> 00:12:48.300
Yusei!

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:56.220
Yusei!

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:05.570
The mark is vanishing.  Did 
something happen to Yusei?

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:09.600
I don't know, but something 
must have happened.

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:18.020
Something happened to Yusei.

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:34.950
The duel was suspended right 
before you would've lost.

00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:38.670
Your D-Wheel's bad performance saved you.

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:45.020
Feel pain!  Be scared!

00:13:45.020 --> 00:13:49.940
Let fear conquer you so that you 
burn in the fires of a living hell!

00:13:49.940 --> 00:13:54.700
You'll face the same hardships that I faced!

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:14.450
You're safe for now.

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:19.020
Until the next time we meet, feel 
the shame while you tremble in fear.

00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:26.100
Yusei!

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:27.480
Yusei!

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:28.330
Yusei!

00:14:28.460 --> 00:14:30.830
Hang in there!  Are you okay, Yusei?

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:34.150
This is bad.

00:14:34.150 --> 00:14:35.850
Yusei, pull yourself together!

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:37.020
Don't touch him!

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:39.230
Hurry and put him on!

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:40.580
Crow!

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:42.550
I'll take him to Martha's place!

00:14:42.550 --> 00:14:43.910
Martha's place?

00:14:43.910 --> 00:14:45.130
The House?

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:47.340
Yeah.  You come later!

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:52.170
Yusei…

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:56.990
Hey, pilot!  Hurry up 
and land the helicopter!

00:14:56.990 --> 00:14:59.750
Immediately return to the City!

00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:03.920
Stop messing around!  You're 
going to abandon Yusei?

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:09.770
Master Atlas, what can you do when 
you don't have a D-Wheel right now?

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:18.490
What should we do?

00:15:18.490 --> 00:15:21.790
There's only one thing to do.  
Let's go to the House right away.

00:15:22.960 --> 00:15:24.770
Wait a second.

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:26.970
What is it?

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:29.100
We have to take this with us.

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:33.190
C'mon, Rally.  Are you seriously thinking 
of pushing that all the way to the House?

00:15:33.190 --> 00:15:38.720
There are lots of thieves up 
ahead.  If we take that with us...

00:15:38.720 --> 00:15:41.990
That's an even greater reason 
why we can't leave this here!

00:15:41.990 --> 00:15:46.540
Did you forget that this 
treasure is important to us?

00:15:48.850 --> 00:15:53.260
You're right.  It's an important 
bond between us and Yusei.

00:15:53.710 --> 00:16:01.020
We all gathered parts that we thought were 
useful, and then we brought them to Yusei.

00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:07.510
Yeah, and we were so happy when we built it.

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:08.840
Yeah.

00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:11.740
It's because we all did it together.

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:14.480
Let's take it with us!

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:17.130
Yeah!  It's the symbol of our friendship.

00:16:17.130 --> 00:16:18.440
And our bond!

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:19.740
Thank you!

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:21.410
All right!

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:24.790
It's not my fault if something bad happens!

00:16:37.070 --> 00:16:40.000
Doesn't this area seem really dangerous?

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:42.100
This isn't the time to be scared.

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:46.190
That's right!  You knew the consequences!

00:16:49.030 --> 00:16:50.340
They showed up!

00:16:56.270 --> 00:16:57.830
Who are you?

00:16:57.830 --> 00:17:00.070
What kind of greeting is that?

00:17:00.070 --> 00:17:01.850
You're the trespassers.

00:17:01.850 --> 00:17:04.670
But it looks like you brought 
something interesting.

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:09.980
Don't come near us!  Don't touch 
this with your dirty hands!

00:17:09.980 --> 00:17:13.170
Nerve, stop it!  You're only riling them up!

00:17:16.020 --> 00:17:17.820
I told you so!

00:17:17.820 --> 00:17:23.490
Forget what I said.  We're in a hurry, 
so can you please let us pass?

00:17:23.490 --> 00:17:26.570
Then pay the toll.

00:17:26.570 --> 00:17:28.430
A toll?

00:17:28.430 --> 00:17:32.310
Yeah.  Leave that behind.

00:17:32.310 --> 00:17:36.330
You must be kidding!  We won't 
even give you one screw!

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:40.310
Then leave your cards behind.  
You must have those.

00:17:40.310 --> 00:17:43.610
No way!  You can't have our cards either!

00:17:43.610 --> 00:17:46.750
If you don't, we'll take both.

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:48.340
What should we do?

00:17:48.340 --> 00:17:49.860
I don't know.

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:52.600
Our cards aren't as important 
as Yusei's D-Wheel.

00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:55.280
Everyone, take out all your cards.

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:56.720
Dammit!

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:00.280
Take 'em!

00:18:02.590 --> 00:18:04.850
Now's our chance!

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:15.800
That went well.

00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:18.190
It looks like we gave them the slip.

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:23.030
Pay the toll.

00:18:23.030 --> 00:18:25.240
Another group appeared!

00:18:25.240 --> 00:18:27.340
What should we do?  We 
don't have any cards left.

00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:29.480
Dammit, in that case…

00:18:31.310 --> 00:18:32.100
Take 'em!

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:36.030
Now's our chance!

00:18:44.860 --> 00:18:46.430
Martha!

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:50.090
It's me!  Hurry up and open the door!

00:18:50.090 --> 00:18:52.650
Who is it?  It's the middle of the night.

00:18:53.950 --> 00:18:54.990
Crow!

00:18:54.990 --> 00:18:56.660
Martha, big trouble!

00:18:58.020 --> 00:18:59.480
Yusei!

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:02.300
What happened?

00:19:03.170 --> 00:19:05.270
This is bad.

00:19:05.300 --> 00:19:10.880
Anyone!  Help me carry Yusei inside!

00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:15.850
Hang in there!  I'll save you, Yusei!

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:25.640
I'm dying.

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:27.840
Let's rest for a little while.

00:19:27.840 --> 00:19:29.200
Yeah.

00:19:29.970 --> 00:19:32.370
Why are you complaining?

00:19:32.630 --> 00:19:36.510
The person who's in the 
most trouble is Yusei!

00:19:36.510 --> 00:19:39.380
And we're the ones who are going to rest?

00:19:40.260 --> 00:19:45.120
We promised to protect this 
D-Wheel, no matter what!

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:46.190
Rally…

00:19:46.190 --> 00:19:53.920
You're right.  We can't be the ones 
to give up when Yusei is hurting.

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:58.400
Yeah, we have to bring this 
symbol of friendship to Yusei.

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:01.340
Let's go to Yusei!

00:20:02.270 --> 00:20:06.180
But wait.  Even if we want to go…

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:08.970
It's a dead end!

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:11.010
What should we do?

00:20:11.010 --> 00:20:13.030
Are you in trouble?

00:20:13.030 --> 00:20:14.500
Another one showed up!

00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:17.020
We can't pay any more tolls!

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:19.280
I don't need that.

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:22.260
There's a path over there.

00:20:22.760 --> 00:20:23.880
He's right.

00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:27.950
I'll help you.

00:20:29.280 --> 00:20:30.740
This way.

00:20:30.740 --> 00:20:34.220
This way.

00:20:35.050 --> 00:20:38.020
Thank goodness that there are 
nice people in this area.

00:20:38.020 --> 00:20:40.600
This way!

00:20:46.480 --> 00:20:47.910
Now!

00:20:50.330 --> 00:20:51.740
The D-Wheel!

00:20:51.740 --> 00:20:53.340
Our symbol of friendship!

00:20:53.340 --> 00:20:54.740
Help us!

00:20:56.210 --> 00:20:57.380
What is that?

00:20:57.670 --> 00:21:03.490
This is Security!  Leave 
that D-Wheel and surrender!

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:05.460
Security!

00:21:05.940 --> 00:21:08.170
Scatter!

00:21:09.070 --> 00:21:11.440
This is what it means to 
have a savior in hell.

00:21:11.440 --> 00:21:12.790
Thank goodness!

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:14.760
Security is everywhere.

00:21:14.760 --> 00:21:18.640
But Security isn't supposed 
to come all the way out here.

00:21:18.640 --> 00:21:20.420
Then who is it?

00:21:26.830 --> 00:21:28.480
Saiga!

00:21:28.480 --> 00:21:32.250
That's an interesting choice 
of clothing.  What happened?

00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:33.530
Well...

00:21:33.530 --> 00:21:35.120
Yusei was…

00:21:49.670 --> 00:21:52.430
Yusei, hang in there!

00:22:14.160 --> 00:22:18.630
We look up and vow towards the shining light

00:22:18.990 --> 00:22:23.700
We will build our own future

00:22:24.170 --> 00:22:29.140
The far dawn shines blindingly

00:22:29.610 --> 00:22:34.320
Awaken in the wonderland

00:22:39.920 --> 00:22:49.460
The overflowing wave of emotions approaches

00:22:49.890 --> 00:22:55.030
This world can’t be solved using algorithms

00:22:55.100 --> 00:22:59.740
Even if it loses its light

00:23:00.200 --> 00:23:05.010
The hourglass behind the 
heart can’t be turned

00:23:05.010 --> 00:23:09.480
Roll the dice and get 
out and follow the light

00:23:09.680 --> 00:23:15.060
Fly towards tomorrow faster than a heartbeat

00:23:15.180 --> 00:23:19.860
This journey has no end

00:23:20.160 --> 00:23:25.400
There’s no meaning 
because there are no tears

00:23:25.830 --> 00:23:30.640
Hear my voice
